diff --git a/src/nix/top.md b/src/nix/top.md
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/nix/top.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+R"(
+
+# Examples
+
+* Show the active builds:
+
+  ```console
+  # nix top
+  nix top - 14:02:17  2 builds, 6 processes, 812.4% CPU
+  USER          PID   %CPU    TIME  WALL  DERIVATION/COMMAND
+  nixbld11  3534394  790.3  110.2s   48s  /nix/store/lzvdxlbr6xjd9w8py4nd2y2nnqb9gz7p-nix-util-tests-3.13.2.drv
+  nixbld11  3534394    0.0    0.8s        └───bash -e /nix/store/jwqf79v5p51x9mv8vx20fv9mzm2x7kig-source-stdenv.sh
+  nixbld11  3534751    1.5   36.3s            └───ninja -j24
+  nixbld11  3535637   98.0    4.1s                ├───/nix/store/0v2jfvx71l1zn14l97pznvbqnhiq3pyd-gcc-14.3.0/bin/g++ -fPIC
+  nixbld11  3535658   99.5    3.0s                └───/nix/store/0v2jfvx71l1zn14l97pznvbqnhiq3pyd-gcc-14.3.0/bin/g++ -fPIC
+  nixbld1   3534377   22.1    1.8s    5s  /nix/store/nh2dx9cqcy9lw4d4rvd0dbsflwdsbzdy-patchelf-0.18.0.drv
+  nixbld1   3534377    0.0    1.8s        └───bash -e /nix/store/xk05lkk4ij6pc7anhdbr81appiqbcb01-default-builder.sh
+  ```
+
+# Description
+
+This command shows the currently running Nix builds in a continuously updating full-screen view, similar to
+`top`. It shows the same information as [`nix ps`](./nix3-ps.md), plus the CPU usage of each build and
+process since the previous update.
+
+The columns are:
+
+* `USER`: The user that the process runs as.
+* `PID`: The process ID.
+* `%CPU`: CPU usage since the previous update. 100% corresponds to one fully used CPU core.
+* `TIME`: Total CPU time consumed. For a process, this includes the CPU time of its reaped children.
+* `WALL`: How long the build has been running.
+* `DERIVATION/COMMAND`: The derivation being built, or the command line of a process in the build.
+
+The following keys are supported:
+
+* `q`, `Ctrl-C`: Quit.
+* `↑`/`↓`, `k`/`j`: Scroll one line.
+* `PgUp`/`PgDn`: Scroll one page.
+* `Home`/`End`, `g`/`G`: Scroll to the top or bottom.
+* `t`, `Enter`: Toggle between showing the processes of each build and showing only the builds.
+* `s`: Cycle the sort order of builds: by CPU usage, by wall time, or by name.
+* `+`/`-`: Increase or decrease the refresh interval by 0.5 seconds (default 2 seconds).
+* `Space`: Refresh now.
+* `Ctrl-L`: Redraw the screen.
+
+)"
